// Title: Suspicious UltraVNC Execution
// Sigma ID: 871b9555-69ca-4993-99d3-35a59f9f3599
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Bhabesh Raj
// Date: 2022-03-04 | Modified: 2022-03-09
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, G0047, T1021.005
// Description: Detects suspicious UltraVNC command line flag combination that indicate a auto reconnect upon
//   execution, e.g. startup (as seen being used by Gamaredon threat group)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20220224045756/https://www.ria.ee/sites/default/files/content-editors/kuberturve/tale_of_gamaredon_infection.pdf
//   - https://symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com/blogs/threat-intelligence/shuckworm-gamaredon-espionage-ukraine
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/unit-42-title-gamaredon-group-toolset-evolution
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20240528223522/https://uvnc.com/docs/uvnc-viewer/52-ultravnc-viewer-commandline-parameters.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ultravnc_susp_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-autoreconnect " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-connect " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-id:"
